From fb83343c1087d1ecae6642551511773fb39078c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:58:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [DVBridge] The active area of a picture, read as the
 serializer reads its level 5 block

dvbridge_l5_area() gives the active area of a picture, in its own samples, from its Dolby Vision
metadata: the level 5 offsets read exactly as the serializer of native output reads them
(dvbridge_dv_margins(): as offsets of the picture, or as those of a 3840x2160 master that the
picture was cropped or scaled from, each side taking the smaller margin, so that a wrong reading
can only leave a part of the bars in, never take picture out). It calls that function itself, on
the picture placed as native output places a picture drawn whole at its own shape (at its own size
where it fits in 3840x2160; a larger one of up to 4096x2304 scaled down, its margins brought back
to its samples), so that Hades has one reading of the block and not a second one that could drift
from it.

Metadata that cannot be read (dvbridge_dv_readable()), a picture of a size the bridge does not
take, no level 5 block, more than one (a frame the serializer refuses), or offsets that fit no
reading give no area and say why, in a fixed text. It also gives the RPU's scene mark
(scene_refresh_flag) and the offsets as the RPU gives them.

For the zoom to the active area in Kodi (ActiveAreaZoom.h), which reads it for each picture queued
while its setting is on; nothing else calls it.
